DTSTAMP:20260428T035242Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T110000
SUMMARY:Rice Pinnacle Bent Creek Trail
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a 5 
 to 5.5 mile hike from the Rice Pinnacle Parking Lot.\n\nThese are 2.7 to 3
  mph hikes. We stop once for water break halfway through. We tend to be do
 ne by 10:50 or 11:00 p.m.. if we stick to 5 miles\,
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/314103952/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260403T110146Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260403T110146Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_314103961@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260428T035242Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T110000
SUMMARY:Craven Gap
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly undulating hike. It's narrow at first with some rocky steps and then 
 narrow and rooty for most of the way until halfway when there's a short cl
 imb to the 2.5 mile mark. We go about 2.7 to 2.9 mph.\n\nWell behaved dogs
  on leashes are welcome to attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel
  lot on the other side of the road\, closest to Town Mountain. You'll see 
 some people gathering by their cars.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are d
 esigned for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably 
 fit. It's not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we ca
 n get our hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversati
 on and meet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce o
 urselves briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is th
 e person who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the p
 arking spot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, bu
 t it's not a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We bas
 ically keep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short
  (approximately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way ba
 ck. If we get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 1
 0:50.\n\nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn a
 round half way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/314103961/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260403T110246Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260403T110246Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
